<title>MEXICO: Mexico to lower steel tariffs on 4 U.S. firms Fri.</title>
<headline>Mexico to lower steel tariffs on 4 U.S. firms Fri.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Trade Ministry said Thursday that it would lower tariffs on four U.S. steel firms from September 27, in keeping with a court order.</p>
<p>The new import tariffs, applying to hot-rolled steel, which will apply following offical publication Friday in the Diario Oficial de la Federacion, the government gazette, are as follows, the ministry said:</p>
<p>    - Bethlehem Steel Corporation 23.7 percent</p>
<p>    - Geneva Steel Company	  26.3 percent</p>
<p>    - USX Corporation		 19.5 percent</p>
<p>    - National Steel Corporation  28.6 percent</p>
<p>It said it was thus complying with a June 24 court order which found that the previous tariffs, set in 1993, were based on reports by authorities who were not qualified to make the relevant verification visits.</p>
<p>The four companies had appealed the tariffs on those grounds.</p>
<p>--Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289558</p>
